    "description": "esm-spec §9.6.1 `reference_only`, §9.6.4 rule 5: the rule `fv_div_edges` (a `where` on edge fields) fires on div(F) but not on div(G), which stays a call; the compound rule `exp`, rooted at the core op `sqrt`, fires on sqrt(x^2). Emit writes both rules match-less and `reference_only`, so on reload neither becomes a callable definition (div(G) stays a call, and `exp` is not refused as a definition of a core operator): emitted.esm re-emits byte for byte.",
    "name": "reference_only_round_trip"
  },
